  "id": "stereotypic-movement-disorder",
  "term": "stereotypic movement disorder",
  "definition": "Stereotypic movement disorder is a condition marked by repetitive, seemingly driven movements that have no clear function. These behaviors significantly disrupt normal activity or can lead to serious self-inflicted injury, and are not explained by a substance or a general medical condition.",
